#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:5
#: bb82474aee8441f08dcd9d5976d16740
msgid "Choosing an Autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:7
#: 711992d090a74d9fabef5e70db75f6ec
msgid "ArduPilot runs on many different autopilot boards. Selecting the right board depends on the physical constraints of the vehicle, features desired, and the applications that you want to run. Factors to consider are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:11
#: 3c95202c9dc941309a43be031bd27f77
msgid "Sensor Redundancy: ArduPilot supports redundant IMUS, GPS, etc. Many controllers have multiple IMUs integrated on board for applications requiring this level of reliability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:12
#: 2aa47850dccc4e7e9d4a7f699dac94b3
msgid "Number of Servo/Motor Outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:13
#: 2a6bc116669045ae863835f5fd20d8cc
msgid "Number of UARTs: Telemetry radios, GPS's, Companion Computers, etc can be attached via these ports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:14
#: 534b61ab99134deb8476fd3ca9e7a0f2
msgid "External Buses: I2C, CAN, etc. allow many types of devices, such as airspeed sensors, LED controllers, etc. to be attached to the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:15
#: 2af58de356d2409ba2375c1686806e27
msgid "Number of Analog I/O: Some controllers have analog I/O available for such features as inputting receiver signal strength (RSSI) or battery voltage/current or other analog sensors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:16
#: 9bb05a1be46c4ed3bd5bd7d4eb2a4453
msgid "Integrated Features: Such as on-board OSD (On Screen Display), integrated battery monitoring sensors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:17
#: 72540fc14e734211beb93d61bd3a9521
msgid "Vibration Isolation: Internal mechanical vibration isolators for IMUs for high vibration applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:18
#: f99f49514f0c48e1b8a868f3d9d876bc
msgid "IMU Heaters: On board temperature control of IMUs for applications in harsh environments or widely varying temperatures during a flight to provide the highest possible precision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:19
#: e317a1455cfa4e73a6dbb817074a51d4
msgid "Size: Many vehicles have limited space for the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:20
#: ed6df9e1a40346e1826e96a73ff54369
msgid "Expense: Controller prices range from ~$25 to much more, depending on feature set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:22
#: 0beb6fd4385941d0b67c9d99746397bb
msgid "The sections below provide information about ArduPilot autopilot hardware options.  The list below is sorted by manufacturer and product name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:26
#: e71f44486c084c7b93a9a224fd09fb03
msgid "There are also numerous clones and minor variants of the boards linked below. Many of these may be perfectly capable replacements. Help in selecting an autopilot can also be obtained in the user forums (`ArduPilot Discuss <https://discuss.ardupilot.org>`__ or `RC Groups <https://www.rcgroups.com/forums/showthread.php?3102183-Most-Integrated-Ardupilot-Flight-Controller-%28ChiBios%29>`__ )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:33
#: 8bc7dde9af73454da6bc84dc31e1fe74
msgid "Not all of these autopilots have been directly tested by ArduPilot development team members and while firmware  is provided by ArduPilot, it does not constitute an endorsement by ArduPilot.  However, most boards developed by ArduPilot Partners have been provided to the ArduPilot development team to aid in any possible support issues that might arise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:35
#: 96847a5af53e4fca993e6e13f4c94709
msgid "Due to flash memory limitations, most F4 based, and some other boards, do not include all ArduPilot features. See :ref:`Firmware Limitations <common-limited_firmware>` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:38
